{
  "id": "COMPOUND:19069 - PROTEIN:518",
  "verbalization": "Scillarenin 3-O-rhamnoside is shown to interact with Protein-arginine deiminase type-1 through a series of target relationships, with Protein-arginine deiminase type-3 acting as a central intermediary. This pathway involves the enzyme Protein-arginine deiminase type-3, which is targeted by multiple compounds, including Scillarenin 3-O-rhamnoside, and in turn, is targeted by other molecules such as 1,1-Dimethoxycyclohexane and 1,1,2-Trimethyl-3,5-bis(1-methylethenyl)cyclohexane. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of arginine metabolism, a process that is central to the function of Protein-arginine deiminase type-1. The evidence suggests a mechanistic link between Scillarenin 3-O-rhamnoside and Protein-arginine deiminase type-1, likely through the inhibition of a key enzyme in the arginine metabolism pathway. The consistent presence of Protein-arginine deiminase type-3 as a target in multiple pathways supports the hypothesis that Scillarenin 3-O-rhamnoside may modulate this enzyme, potentially through a mechanism involving the inhibition of its activity or the regulation of its expression. The integrated evidence highlights the importance of this enzyme in the metabolic regulation of arginine, and the observed interactions suggest a plausible biological mechanism by which Scillarenin 3-O-rhamnoside may exert its effects.",
